1
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:03,420
Hey, guys.

2
00:00:03,462 --> 00:00:04,171
All:
Hey.

3
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:08,383
So... what do you think?

4
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:09,635
About what?

5
00:00:09,677 --> 00:00:10,302
Yeah, what?
What?

6
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:11,178
Huh?

7
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:12,179
Are you kidding?

8
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,514
Okay, I'll give you a hint.

9
00:00:13,555 --> 00:00:14,890
I'll give you a hint.

10
00:00:17,017 --> 00:00:18,686
Eyes.

11
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:20,646
No, no. Your eyes.

12
00:00:20,688 --> 00:00:22,564
No. Chandler's eyes!

13
00:00:22,606 --> 00:00:25,526
I got glasses.

14
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:28,111
You-you always had glasses.

15
00:00:29,613 --> 00:00:32,533
No, I didn't.

16
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:35,285
Are you sure?

17
00:00:36,704 --> 00:00:39,039
Yeah. Didn't, didn't you
used to have a pair

18
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,916
that were really
round and burgundy

19
00:00:40,958 --> 00:00:42,918
and they made you
look kind of, um...

20
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:43,919
Feminine.

21
00:00:43,961 --> 00:00:44,920
Yes.

22
00:00:44,962 --> 00:00:46,380
No.

23
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:48,047
Sweetie, I think
the glasses look great.

24
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,383
They make you look really sexy.

25
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:50,175
Really?

26
00:00:50,217 --> 00:00:51,050
Yeah.

27
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:52,051
You didn't think

28
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:53,387
I used to wear glasses, right?

29
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:54,763
Of course.

30
00:00:54,805 --> 00:00:56,932
( mouthing ):
I didn't know it.

31
00:01:03,856 --> 00:01:08,068
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

32
00:01:08,109 --> 00:01:11,321
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

33
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:14,700
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

34
00:01:14,742 --> 00:01:18,913
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

35
00:01:18,954 --> 00:01:21,248
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

36
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:24,083
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

37
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:27,462
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

38
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:29,798
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

39
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,967
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

40
00:01:32,009 --> 00:01:34,261
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

41
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:37,431
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

42
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:43,520
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

43
00:01:51,403 --> 00:01:54,281
So, what do you guys want
for an engagement present?

44
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:55,616
That's okay, Pheebs.

45
00:01:55,657 --> 00:01:56,992
We're not having
a party or anything

46
00:01:57,034 --> 00:01:58,285
so you don't
have to get us...

47
00:01:58,326 --> 00:01:59,453
Bup-bup-bup!

48
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:01,413
Someone wants
to give us a present

49
00:02:01,455 --> 00:02:03,832
we don't want
to deprive them of that joy.

50
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:05,709
Oh, you know what
you should get them?

51
00:02:05,751 --> 00:02:07,711
One of those little
portable CD players.

52
00:02:07,753 --> 00:02:09,421
Oh, I already
have one.

53
00:02:09,463 --> 00:02:13,092
Not unless someone borrowed it
and left it at the gynecologist.

54
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:19,473
Yeah, and-and by "someone,"
she means Joey.

55
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:21,308
Hey, I know what I want.

56
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:23,226
What we want, honey.

57
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:24,352
No, no, you don't want this.

58
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:25,646
No, I want to have

59
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:27,982
your grandmother's
cookie recipe.

60
00:02:28,023 --> 00:02:30,525
You mean the chocolate chip
cookie recipe?

61
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:31,610
Uh-huh, yeah.

62
00:02:31,652 --> 00:02:33,236
You mean the one

63
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:35,114
that my grandmother made me
swear on her deathbed

64
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:37,074
that I would never let out
of our family?

65
00:02:37,116 --> 00:02:40,953
Dying people say
the craziest things.

66
00:02:40,995 --> 00:02:43,288
I've wanted it for years.

67
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:45,833
I was going to make
cookies for my children.

68
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:47,960
Well, break my heart.

69
00:02:48,002 --> 00:02:49,503
Oh, all right.

70
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:51,130
Okay. I'm going
to be the mom

71
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:53,841
who makes the world's best
chocolate chip cookies.

72
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:57,636
Our kids are going
to be fat, aren't they?

73
00:02:57,678 --> 00:02:59,262
Ahoy!

74
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:00,263
All:
Hey.

75
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:01,723
How's the boat?

76
00:03:01,765 --> 00:03:03,182
Great. I'm really getting into
this sailing stuff.

77
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:05,226
Oh, so you finally took it
out of the marina, huh?

78
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:07,521
Why would I do that?

79
00:03:07,562 --> 00:03:10,899
It took three guys
to get the thing in there.

80
00:03:10,941 --> 00:03:13,777
Well, if you don't sail your
boat, what do you do on it?

81
00:03:13,819 --> 00:03:14,736
Well, it's great.

82
00:03:14,778 --> 00:03:15,988
It's a great place

83
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:17,656
to just kind of sit,
hang around

84
00:03:17,698 --> 00:03:19,992
drink a few beers,
eat some chips.

85
00:03:20,034 --> 00:03:23,704
Well, it's good
that you finally have
a place to do that.

86
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:25,914
You know, Joey,
I could teach you

87
00:03:25,956 --> 00:03:27,415
to sail if you want.

88
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:28,709
You could?

89
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,711
Yeah. I've been sailing
my whole life.

90
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:33,212
When I was 15,
my dad bought me my own boat.

91
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:34,464
What?

92
00:03:34,506 --> 00:03:35,423
Your own boat?

93
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:36,299
What? What?

94
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:37,216
He was trying to cheer me up.

95
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:38,552
My pony was sick.

96
00:03:49,228 --> 00:03:51,148
You know what
I was thinking?

97
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:52,357
What?

98
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:55,027
Nothing. I just like
to go like this.

99
00:03:55,069 --> 00:03:57,612
Hey, Chandler,
what are you doing tonight?

100
00:03:57,654 --> 00:03:58,947
Uh, Why?
Do you have a lecture?

101
00:03:58,989 --> 00:03:59,948
No. Why?

102
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:01,533
Then free as a bird.

103
00:04:01,575 --> 00:04:02,701
What's up?

104
00:04:02,743 --> 00:04:04,119
My dad wanted to know

105
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:05,662
if you want to play
racquetball with us.

106
00:04:05,704 --> 00:04:06,663
Wow, that's great.

107
00:04:06,705 --> 00:04:07,873
Dad must really like you.

108
00:04:07,915 --> 00:04:09,541
He doesn't ask
just anyone to play.

109
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:11,543
Yeah, and he didn't
really ask for you.

110
00:04:11,585 --> 00:04:12,878
He asked for Chauncey.

111
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,629
I assumed he meant you.

112
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,590
Well, did-did you
correct him?

113
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:19,384
No. I-I thought
it'd be more fun this way.

114
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:20,802
That is so cool.

115
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:23,304
Maybe this is something
you could do every week.

116
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:25,182
Or you could sit with
him on the front porch

117
00:04:25,224 --> 00:04:27,101
and make sure no one
steals the trash cans.

118
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:29,895
He does that
every week, too. Hmm.

119
00:04:29,937 --> 00:04:33,148
Oh, just so you know,
y-you have to let him win.

120
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:34,524
He hates to lose.

121
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:35,734
Oh, no problem.

122
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:37,694
Maybe I'll play
with my left hand.

123
00:04:37,736 --> 00:04:40,155
You're not a lefty?

124
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:43,366
Does anybody know me?

125
00:04:46,870 --> 00:04:48,163
( sighs irately )

126
00:04:48,205 --> 00:04:49,998
What's wrong, Phoebe?

127
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:53,001
I just went to my old
apartment to get you
the-the cookie recipe

128
00:04:53,043 --> 00:04:55,670
and that stupid fire
burned it up.

129
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:57,839
No! Why didn't you
make a copy

130
00:04:57,881 --> 00:04:59,674
and-and keep it
in a fireproof box

131
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:01,676
and keep it at least
a hundred yards

132
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:03,011
away from the original?

133
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:11,311
Because I'm normal.

134
00:05:12,938 --> 00:05:15,774
But that was the one legacy
my grandmother left me

135
00:05:15,816 --> 00:05:18,693
and I know you wanted it
as an engagement present.

136
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:21,071
What? We have to get you
an engagement present?

137
00:05:21,113 --> 00:05:23,282
Don't worry
about it, Pheebs.

138
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:26,201
No one got me
an engagement present.

139
00:05:26,243 --> 00:05:30,205
Okay, here.
I don't have the recipe, but...

140
00:05:30,247 --> 00:05:32,874
Here, I wish you health
and happiness.

141
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:35,127
An old cookie?

142
00:05:35,169 --> 00:05:37,712
See, this is what happens

143
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:40,465
when you don't register
for gifts.

144
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:43,218
See, no, I-I made a batch
and I froze it

145
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:45,386
and this is the only one left.

146
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:46,847
We can't accept this.

147
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:48,056
Why not?

148
00:05:48,098 --> 00:05:50,058
Because it's gross.

149
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:51,559
No... wait.

150
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:54,271
I think I can figure out
the recipe from this cookie.

151
00:05:54,313 --> 00:05:56,564
I do stuff like this
at work all the time.

152
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:58,317
Really?
Yeah. I think
I can do it.

153
00:05:58,357 --> 00:05:59,276
Oh, yay!

154
00:06:03,197 --> 00:06:05,199
Okay, Ross,
we owe you a present.

155
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,993
Two! I've been engaged twice.

156
00:06:16,043 --> 00:06:17,336
Look at this clown.

157
00:06:17,376 --> 00:06:19,378
Just 'cause he got
a bigger boat

158
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,798
he thinks he can take
up the whole river.

159
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:24,425
Get out of the way, jackass!

160
00:06:26,261 --> 00:06:29,097
Who names their boat
Coast Guard, anyway, geez.

161
00:06:31,516 --> 00:06:33,560
That is the Coast Guard.

162
00:06:33,601 --> 00:06:35,312
What are they
doing out here?

163
00:06:35,354 --> 00:06:37,272
Coast is all the
way over there.

164
00:06:37,314 --> 00:06:39,649
Joe-Joey, just ignore
the boats, all right?

165
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:42,110
All right.
We're not finished
with our lesson yet.

166
00:06:42,152 --> 00:06:44,529
I'm just going over the basic
points one more time. Ready?

167
00:06:44,571 --> 00:06:46,865
Oh, come on, Rach, not again.
I got it, okay?

168
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:49,326
Let's start sailing,
and I want to go over there

169
00:06:49,368 --> 00:06:51,703
where that boatload of girls is.
Yeah! Ho-ho!

170
00:06:51,745 --> 00:06:53,788
Oh, okay. Is that
what you want to do?

171
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,665
Want to go over

172
00:06:55,707 --> 00:06:58,168
and give a little shout out
to the old hot chicas, huh?

173
00:06:58,210 --> 00:07:00,170
Okay. Let's do that, Sailor Joe.

174
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:01,546
Quick question, though.

175
00:07:01,588 --> 00:07:03,048
What's this called?

176
00:07:03,090 --> 00:07:05,800
Uh... boat rope?

177
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:07,510
Wrong.

178
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:09,346
How do you get
the main sail up?

179
00:07:09,388 --> 00:07:10,389
Uh...

180
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:12,640
Rub it?

181
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:16,353
No.

182
00:07:16,395 --> 00:07:19,147
What do you do if I say
we are coming about?

183
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:21,482
I'd say... come again?

184
00:07:21,524 --> 00:07:24,485
No, no. I-I know this one,
I know this one. Uh...

185
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:26,571
( air horn honks )

186
00:07:26,613 --> 00:07:28,573
Time's up. Now you're dead.

187
00:07:28,615 --> 00:07:30,117
And deaf.

188
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:32,160
Okay, you just go on and make
your little jokey jokes

189
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:34,955
but if you do not know
what you are doing out at sea

190
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:36,123
you will die at sea.

191
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:38,125
Am I getting through
to you, sailor?!

192
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,126
Yes.

193
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:40,460
Don't just say yes.

194
00:07:40,501 --> 00:07:41,711
This isn't a game.

195
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:43,964
Joey, you could really
get hurt out here.

196
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:47,550
Okay, so you want
to pay attention
or do you want to die?

197
00:07:49,552 --> 00:07:53,014
I want to make a ship-to-shore
call to Chandler.

198
00:08:01,315 --> 00:08:03,275
I-I definitely taste nutmeg.

199
00:08:03,317 --> 00:08:04,567
You do?

200
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:05,902
You don't?

201
00:08:05,944 --> 00:08:07,612
Huh. Well, that's
the difference

202
00:08:07,654 --> 00:08:09,614
between a professional
and a layman.

203
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:12,993
Yeah. That and arrogance.

204
00:08:14,995 --> 00:08:16,204
Hey.

205
00:08:16,246 --> 00:08:17,956
Hey. How was sailing?

206
00:08:17,998 --> 00:08:19,624
I don't want to talk about it.

207
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:21,126
Oh, you know, you could have

208
00:08:21,168 --> 00:08:22,752
at least saved me
a whole cookie.

209
00:08:22,794 --> 00:08:24,921
Both:
No, no, no, no!

210
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:29,676
Women are mean!

211
00:08:34,014 --> 00:08:35,598
I can't believe that.

212
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,934
Well, now the only
thing that's left

213
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:41,729
of my grandmother's
legacy is... this crumb.

214
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:45,733
I wish you a long
and happy marriage.

215
00:08:47,486 --> 00:08:49,237
Hey.

216
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:50,613
Hey. How was it?

217
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:52,740
Well, I had
a great time.

218
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:55,869
Um, Chauncey,
on the other hand...

219
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:58,163
I will tell the story.

220
00:08:58,205 --> 00:08:59,498
It was going great.

221
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:00,499
I let him win.

222
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:01,875
We were bonding.

223
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:03,626
He even said
that I could call him Dad.

224
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:05,670
And what did he ask you
not to call him?

225
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:08,673
Daddy.

226
00:09:08,715 --> 00:09:11,009
All right, look,
here's the story.

227
00:09:11,051 --> 00:09:14,012
Well, we had just finished
playing racquetball

228
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:16,264
and we were going
to take a steam.

229
00:09:16,306 --> 00:09:18,016
I walk into the steam room

230
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:20,394
and it's really steamy.

231
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:25,857
So I take off my glasses
and that's when it happened.

232
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:27,025
Guys?

233
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:28,360
Over here.

234
00:09:28,402 --> 00:09:30,237
Have a seat, son.

235
00:09:35,242 --> 00:09:36,576
Hey!

236
00:09:47,254 --> 00:09:48,380
Oh, my God, Chandler.

237
00:09:48,422 --> 00:09:50,382
I can't believe it.
I know.

238
00:09:50,424 --> 00:09:53,009
You gave my father
a lap dance.

239
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:59,015
Why do they put
so much steam in there?

240
00:09:59,057 --> 00:10:05,313
'Cause otherwise they'd have
to call it the... room room.

241
00:10:05,355 --> 00:10:07,524
Why, okay?

242
00:10:07,566 --> 00:10:08,649
Why?

243
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:11,486
Why did that have to happen?

244
00:10:11,528 --> 00:10:13,321
Come on.
It's not that big a deal.

245
00:10:13,363 --> 00:10:15,365
Not that big a deal?

246
00:10:15,407 --> 00:10:18,535
There... there was touching
of things.

247
00:10:18,577 --> 00:10:21,496
Chandler, I-I know you wanted
to bond with my dad

248
00:10:21,538 --> 00:10:24,291
but did you really have to bond
to that part?

249
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:28,753
Listen, I'm sure that
Dad doesn't care.

250
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:31,005
He probably thought
this was really funny.

251
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:33,049
He'll be telling
this story for years.

252
00:10:33,091 --> 00:10:36,010
I don't want him to tell
this story for years.

253
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:38,555
Oh, but he will.

254
00:10:38,597 --> 00:10:39,722
( chuckles )

255
00:10:39,764 --> 00:10:41,099
He still tells the story

256
00:10:41,141 --> 00:10:43,518
about how Monica tried to escape
from fat camp.

257
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:46,521
I wasn't escaping.

258
00:10:46,563 --> 00:10:48,940
Then how did you get caught
in the barbed wire?

259
00:10:48,982 --> 00:10:51,818
I was trying to help out
a squirrel.

260
00:10:51,859 --> 00:10:53,820
You were trying to eat it.

261
00:10:56,114 --> 00:10:57,574
( phone rings )

262
00:10:57,616 --> 00:11:00,535
If that is your
father calling
to tell this story

263
00:11:00,577 --> 00:11:02,287
then the marriage is off.

264
00:11:02,329 --> 00:11:03,371
Come on.

265
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:04,581
Hello?

266
00:11:04,623 --> 00:11:07,626
I'm sorry. You have
the wrong number.

267
00:11:07,666 --> 00:11:09,794
Okay. I'll call you later, Dad.
I love you.

268
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:17,636
All right. I'm off
to see your dad.

269
00:11:17,676 --> 00:11:18,719
Whoa. Whoa!

270
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,305
Aren't you
a little overdressed?

271
00:11:20,347 --> 00:11:22,015
( laughs )

272
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:25,393
Yeah. And-and you
better make sure
he tips you this time.

273
00:11:25,435 --> 00:11:26,811
( laughing )

274
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:28,813
Oh, look. I figured
I would try to convince him

275
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:30,357
not to tell the story anymore

276
00:11:30,398 --> 00:11:33,193
and I figured the best way
to do that was face-to-face.

277
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:34,319
And by face...

278
00:11:34,361 --> 00:11:35,820
I don't mean his lap.

279
00:11:35,862 --> 00:11:39,115
And by face,
I don't mean my ass.

280
00:11:41,284 --> 00:11:43,328
Hey, are you getting
Monica and Chandler

281
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:44,829
an engagement present?

282
00:11:44,871 --> 00:11:47,248
I don't know. You know,
they didn't get us anything.

283
00:11:47,290 --> 00:11:48,749
Thank you.

284
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:51,461
Hey.

285
00:11:51,503 --> 00:11:52,587
Hey.

286
00:11:52,629 --> 00:11:54,088
Well, hello.

287
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:57,050
So, when are we getting back
out on the water, matey?

288
00:11:57,091 --> 00:11:58,843
Oh, uh...

289
00:11:58,885 --> 00:12:01,513
Well, I don't know the boat way
to say this, but, uh... never.

290
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:04,432
Why not?

291
00:12:04,474 --> 00:12:07,018
Because you're mean on the boat.

292
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:09,521
What? I was just
trying to teach you.

293
00:12:09,563 --> 00:12:10,938
Well, lesson learned.

294
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,106
Rachel is mean.

295
00:12:13,191 --> 00:12:16,152
Yup. Yup-yup-yup-yup-yup.

296
00:12:16,194 --> 00:12:19,322
I remember when she took me
out on her dad's boat.

297
00:12:19,364 --> 00:12:21,575
She wouldn't let me
help out at all.

298
00:12:21,616 --> 00:12:23,117
Oh... excuse me.

299
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:25,995
I wanted you to help, but
you couldn't move your arms

300
00:12:26,037 --> 00:12:28,373
because you were wearing
three life jackets.

301
00:12:28,415 --> 00:12:32,711
You have to respect the sea.

302
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:36,590
Look, Joey, I'm sorry if-if
you thought that was mean

303
00:12:36,631 --> 00:12:39,551
but I got to tell you something:
that was not mean, okay?

304
00:12:39,593 --> 00:12:40,968
My father is mean.

305
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:43,096
He used to yell at me
all the time on the boat.

306
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:44,389
I mean, it was horrible.

307
00:12:44,431 --> 00:12:46,474
I was just being
a really good teacher.

308
00:12:46,516 --> 00:12:49,561
Does a good teacher say,
"Put down the beer, Pinhead"?

309
00:12:49,603 --> 00:12:51,187
Well, does a good student

310
00:12:51,229 --> 00:12:53,814
drink seven beers
during his first lesson?

311
00:12:53,856 --> 00:12:55,483
Six and a half.

312
00:12:55,525 --> 00:12:58,069
You knocked that last one
out of my hand, remember?

313
00:12:58,111 --> 00:13:00,196
Yeah. I didn't want you
to get hit by the boom.

314
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:01,906
Well, it hit me anyway.

315
00:13:01,948 --> 00:13:03,408
And it would have hurt
a lot less

316
00:13:03,450 --> 00:13:05,118
if I'd have finished
that last beer.

317
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:06,703
All right. You know what?

318
00:13:06,745 --> 00:13:08,371
I'm sorry.

319
00:13:08,413 --> 00:13:11,291
I will try to tone it down,
and, uh... stop yelling.

320
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:13,376
You won't boss me around
anymore?

321
00:13:13,418 --> 00:13:14,544
I won't boss you around.

322
00:13:14,586 --> 00:13:15,378
And you'll be nice?

323
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:16,337
And I'll be nice.

324
00:13:16,379 --> 00:13:17,255
And you'll be topless?

325
00:13:17,297 --> 00:13:19,257
And... Joey!

326
00:13:19,299 --> 00:13:20,799
You want me to learn?

327
00:13:25,012 --> 00:13:28,642
Okay. Here's batch 22.

328
00:13:28,683 --> 00:13:30,977
Oh, maybe these will taste
like your grandmother's.

329
00:13:31,018 --> 00:13:33,438
This has a little bit
of orange peel, but no nutmeg.

330
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,523
Let's give it a shot.
Okay. Well...

331
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:36,899
I have not made
this many cookies

332
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:38,234
since I was in the ninth grade.

333
00:13:38,276 --> 00:13:40,027
What was that for,
like, a bake sale?

334
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:42,489
No. Just a Friday night.

335
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,619
Mmm.

336
00:13:47,661 --> 00:13:49,120
These are pretty good.

337
00:13:49,162 --> 00:13:51,247
Yup. But not as good
as batch 17.

338
00:13:51,289 --> 00:13:52,831
Which one was that?

339
00:13:52,873 --> 00:13:54,833
The ones we had right after
you almost threw up.

340
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:56,628
Oh, yeah.

341
00:13:56,670 --> 00:13:58,630
Batch 17 was good.

342
00:13:58,672 --> 00:14:02,467
I did not like batch 16.

343
00:14:02,509 --> 00:14:05,428
( voice croaks ):
I'm okay.

344
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:07,347
Are there any more
from the good batch?

345
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:09,307
'Cause we could just work
off of those.

346
00:14:09,349 --> 00:14:11,267
Yeah... well, yeah,
I think there's one

347
00:14:11,309 --> 00:14:12,560
from batch 17
left, uh...

348
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:18,191
It's batch 16.

349
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:19,275
16, people.

350
00:14:19,317 --> 00:14:21,152
Get out of the way!

351
00:14:26,574 --> 00:14:29,327
Okay, Joey, honey.

352
00:14:29,369 --> 00:14:30,829
You're doing
really good.

353
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:32,831
All right, now.
I'm just going to need you

354
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:34,123
to step
to the port side.

355
00:14:39,671 --> 00:14:42,006
Remember? Remember how we
talked about the port side?

356
00:14:42,048 --> 00:14:43,007
Oh, yeah.

357
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:44,091
Right?

358
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:46,553
No.

359
00:14:46,594 --> 00:14:49,138
It's left, sweetie,
but that's okay.

360
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:50,515
That's a tough one.

361
00:14:50,557 --> 00:14:52,183
I wonder why
you don't just say left.

362
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:54,143
Okay. Go to the left.

363
00:14:54,185 --> 00:14:57,313
( forced laughing )

364
00:14:57,355 --> 00:14:59,023
( clears throat )

365
00:14:59,065 --> 00:15:00,233
The left.
Huh?

366
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:01,693
( yells ):
Just sit over there!

367
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:04,028
Okay. Okay.
You're yelling again. See that?

368
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:05,572
No. No. No, no, no, no.

369
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:08,241
Very quiet, said with love,
no yelling.

370
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:11,703
Well, you know what?

371
00:15:11,745 --> 00:15:13,621
Since I'm here,
I think I'm going to have me

372
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:15,373
a little beer
on the port side.

373
00:15:15,415 --> 00:15:16,624
See what I did there?

374
00:15:16,666 --> 00:15:17,667
Uh-huh.

375
00:15:17,709 --> 00:15:19,210
( forced chuckle )

376
00:15:21,087 --> 00:15:23,089
Okay, Joey,
we're luffing a little bit

377
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:25,132
so will you tighten up
the cunningham?

378
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:26,676
All right, whoa.

379
00:15:26,718 --> 00:15:29,429
You just said a bunch of stuff
I don't know there.

380
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,389
Joey, come on!
We just went over this.

381
00:15:31,431 --> 00:15:33,349
Oh. Oh-oh, you know that...
when we did that

382
00:15:33,391 --> 00:15:34,768
was when that bird

383
00:15:34,809 --> 00:15:37,144
was flying overhead
with the fish in his mouth.

384
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:38,730
Did you see it?
It was gross.

385
00:15:38,772 --> 00:15:39,731
No! All right.

386
00:15:39,773 --> 00:15:40,732
I did not see the bird.

387
00:15:40,774 --> 00:15:41,982
I did not see the fish.

388
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:43,150
I did not see the piece
of Styrofoam

389
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:44,360
that was shaped
like Mike Tyson.

390
00:15:46,237 --> 00:15:49,949
I did not because I was trying
to teach you how to sail a boat

391
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:52,827
which obviously is
an impossible thing to do.

392
00:15:52,869 --> 00:15:54,579
All right. That's it.

393
00:15:54,621 --> 00:15:57,039
You're yelling, and I don't see
you taking your top off. I quit!

394
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:58,165
Well...!

395
00:15:58,207 --> 00:15:59,834
What do you mean, you quit?

396
00:15:59,876 --> 00:16:00,919
You can't quit!

397
00:16:00,959 --> 00:16:02,044
Why not?

398
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:03,797
Because you're
not finished yet

399
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:05,089
and I won't have it.

400
00:16:05,131 --> 00:16:06,299
Greens do not quit.

401
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:07,675
"Greens"?

402
00:16:07,717 --> 00:16:12,513
I'm a Tribbiani,
and Tribbianis quit.

403
00:16:14,641 --> 00:16:15,600
Oh, my God! Wait!

404
00:16:15,642 --> 00:16:17,059
Did I... did I...

405
00:16:17,101 --> 00:16:18,603
I just said, "Greens don't
quit," didn't I?

406
00:16:18,645 --> 00:16:20,271
Did I just say,
"Greens don't quit?!"

407
00:16:20,313 --> 00:16:21,856
Yes. Yes.

408
00:16:21,898 --> 00:16:23,483
Oh, my God.
You did, and you're
still yelling at me.

409
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:25,777
No. No, no.
I'm not yelling at you.

410
00:16:25,819 --> 00:16:27,487
I'm just yelling near you.

411
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:28,529
Oh, God, Joey!

412
00:16:28,571 --> 00:16:29,739
Oh, I'm my father.

413
00:16:29,781 --> 00:16:31,699
Oh, my God!
This is horrible!

414
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:35,536
I've been trying so hard
not to be my mother

415
00:16:35,578 --> 00:16:37,288
I did not see this coming.

416
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:39,791
Oh, Joey...

417
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:42,209
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

418
00:16:42,251 --> 00:16:45,630
I just wanted you to learn.

419
00:16:46,673 --> 00:16:47,882
Oh.

420
00:16:47,924 --> 00:16:50,635
Hey... I did learn.

421
00:16:50,677 --> 00:16:51,761
Really?

422
00:16:51,803 --> 00:16:53,137
Yeah. Come on.

423
00:16:53,179 --> 00:16:54,305
No.

424
00:16:54,347 --> 00:16:56,015
Yeah. It's okay.

425
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:57,308
I know what a mainsail is.

426
00:16:57,350 --> 00:16:59,101
Yeah.

427
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:02,730
Huh? I know... I know to duck
when the boom comes across.

428
00:17:04,315 --> 00:17:05,566
I-I know port is right.

429
00:17:05,608 --> 00:17:06,150
Left.

430
00:17:06,192 --> 00:17:07,735
Damn it!

431
00:17:10,279 --> 00:17:12,365
You know, I bet
it would actually make

432
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:14,032
my grandma really happy

433
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:16,452
to know that we're trying
to figure out her recipe.

434
00:17:16,494 --> 00:17:21,081
I bet she's looking up at us,
and smiling right now.

435
00:17:22,458 --> 00:17:24,502
Looking up?

436
00:17:24,544 --> 00:17:26,212
Oh, yeah.

437
00:17:26,253 --> 00:17:29,340
No, she was really nice to me,
but she's in hell for sure.

438
00:17:31,009 --> 00:17:32,343
Well, I've tried everything.

439
00:17:32,385 --> 00:17:33,970
I give up.
I guess I'm not going to be

440
00:17:34,012 --> 00:17:36,180
the mom who makes the world's
best chocolate chip cookies.

441
00:17:36,222 --> 00:17:41,435
I do make the best...
duck confit with broccoli rabe.

442
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:43,062
( voice breaks ):
Kids love that, right?

443
00:17:44,522 --> 00:17:46,148
Oh, Pheeb, come on.

444
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:48,359
Isn't there any relative
that would have the recipe?

445
00:17:48,401 --> 00:17:50,403
What about... what about
your sister?

446
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:52,112
Oh, no, no. No.

447
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:55,616
I made a promise to myself
that the next time I would talk

448
00:17:55,658 --> 00:17:57,869
to Ursula is over my dead body.

449
00:17:57,911 --> 00:18:02,832
And that's not happening
until October 15, 2032.

450
00:18:02,874 --> 00:18:04,876
That's the day
you're going to die?

451
00:18:04,918 --> 00:18:07,670
See? Darn it.
I've got shuffleboard that day.

452
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:10,256
That's what you think.

453
00:18:14,761 --> 00:18:16,554
Well, what about friends
of your grandmother's?

454
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:17,805
Wouldn't they have the recipe?

455
00:18:17,847 --> 00:18:19,181
Well, you know, I may...

456
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:21,059
I may have relatives
in France who would know.

457
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:24,228
My grandmother said
she got the recipe

458
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:27,398
from her grandmother,
Nestle Toulous.

459
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:30,276
What was her name?

460
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:34,280
Nestle Toulous.

461
00:18:34,321 --> 00:18:37,867
Nestle Tollhouse?

462
00:18:40,787 --> 00:18:42,496
Uh!

463
00:18:42,538 --> 00:18:45,792
You Americans always butcher
the French language.

464
00:18:47,085 --> 00:18:50,254
Phoebe, is this the recipe?

465
00:18:52,130 --> 00:18:54,133
Yes!

466
00:18:55,927 --> 00:18:58,429
Oh! Oh...

467
00:18:58,471 --> 00:19:00,098
I cannot believe
that I just spent

468
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:02,725
the last two days trying
to figure out that recipe

469
00:19:02,767 --> 00:19:04,811
and it was in my cupboard
the whole time.

470
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:06,270
I know!

471
00:19:06,312 --> 00:19:08,940
You see, it is
stuff like this

472
00:19:08,982 --> 00:19:12,318
which is why
you're burning in hell!

473
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:17,031
Chandler:
Just so you understand

474
00:19:17,073 --> 00:19:18,491
I'd feel a lot more comfortable

475
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:20,451
if you didn't tell people
what happened, you know?

476
00:19:20,493 --> 00:19:22,578
I'm a little... I'm a little
embarrassed about it.

477
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:25,039
I understand completely.

478
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:27,792
There's nothing more horrifying
than embarrassing yourself

479
00:19:27,834 --> 00:19:29,168
in front of your in-laws.

480
00:19:29,209 --> 00:19:32,212
As a matter of fact,
when I started dating Judy

481
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:34,298
I was unemployed,
and her father asked me

482
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:37,135
what I did for a living,
and I told him I was a lawyer.

483
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:39,637
What-what did you do
when they found out?

484
00:19:39,679 --> 00:19:41,388
They never did.

485
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:44,642
If you ever see me giving them
legal advice, just nod along.

486
00:19:45,643 --> 00:19:47,520
Shall we?

487
00:20:02,284 --> 00:20:05,412
So... I guess
we wear swimsuits in here.

488
00:20:17,550 --> 00:20:20,803
Well, Joey,
I hate to admit it

489
00:20:20,845 --> 00:20:23,723
but your way of sailing
is a lot more fun.

490
00:20:23,764 --> 00:20:26,017
Yup. Yup.

491
00:20:26,059 --> 00:20:29,562
Hey, why don't you
give a pull on that rope?

492
00:20:29,603 --> 00:20:31,313
Oh, we're not sailing.

493
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,815
Just pull on it.

494
00:20:32,857 --> 00:20:34,274
All right.

495
00:20:35,985 --> 00:20:37,695
Hey!

496
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:39,072
Huh?

497
00:20:39,113 --> 00:20:40,823
Sandwiches!

498
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:42,033
What else?

499
00:20:42,075 --> 00:20:43,659
( chuckles )

500
00:20:43,701 --> 00:20:45,119
Here you go.

501
00:20:45,161 --> 00:20:46,370
Thank you.

502
00:20:46,412 --> 00:20:47,580
Oh, wow!

503
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:51,876
Oop....

504
00:20:51,918 --> 00:20:52,459
What are you doing?

505
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:53,377
Sorry.

506
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:54,503
What... don't hold
it like that.

507
00:20:54,545 --> 00:20:56,254
You're letting all
the good stuff fall out.

508
00:20:56,296 --> 00:20:58,256
Oh. Oop.
Careful!

509
00:20:58,298 --> 00:21:02,011
You're wasting
good pastrami!

510
00:21:02,053 --> 00:21:03,303
( gasps )

511
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:04,764
Oh, my God!

512
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,640
I'm my dad!

